From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: brennoflavio <contato@brennoflavio.com.br>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 16:49:45 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] http: align default fetch header order with Chrome

Serialize non-internal fetch headers in the order observed in local
Chrome 154 recorder captures. Reuse the navigation serializer with a
fetch-specific sequence, materializing implicit Accept and the supported
Accept-Encoding list at their intended positions. Keep native curl
response decoding enabled and preserve explicit values, empty values,
source precedence and trailing custom headers without duplicates.

Leave navigation order, internal requests, XHR, HTTP/1.1 keep-alive,
HTTP/2 pseudo-headers/priorities, TLS and the macOS Chrome 155 persona
unchanged. Compression advertising remains deflate, gzip, br; no zstd
support is claimed or added.

Validation: ReleaseFast build; all 1658 upstream tests; Zig formatting
and harness TypeScript checks. Recorder comparisons cover Chrome, the
previous binary and this change: 54 page visits, 108 selected requests,
HTTP/2, HTTP/1.1 ALPN and no-ALPN fallback, cold and opted-in navigation.
All 18 fetch header-name/casing/order comparisons match Chrome; request
header values, navigation ordering and the previous binary's HTTP/2
summaries are unchanged. Temporary wire diagnostics pass 30 checks per
binary across 20 requests on one reused connection, including author/CDP
overrides, empty headers, redirect retention, HEAD/POST, XHR and native
gzip/deflate/Brotli decoding. The repeated TLS gate passes all eight
scenarios with 20 processes per browser. Reviewer found no issues.
No new unit tests.

References: fingerprint/README.md; patches/0057; pinned curl 8.22.0.
---
 src/network/HttpClient.zig | 29 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/network/HttpClient.zig b/src/network/HttpClient.zig
index 4c9bee4..4caf9b5 100644
--- a/src/network/HttpClient.zig
+++ b/src/network/HttpClient.zig
@@ -3690,8 +3690,8 @@ pub const Transfer = struct {
         // accumulate duplicates.
         conn.clearHeaders();
         const arena = self.arena.allocator();
-        if (!req.internal and req.request_mode == .navigate) {
-            const order = [_][]const u8{
+        if (!req.internal and (req.request_mode == .navigate or req.resource_type == .fetch)) {
+            const order: []const []const u8 = if (req.request_mode == .navigate) &.{
                 "sec-ch-ua",
                 "sec-ch-ua-mobile",
                 "sec-ch-ua-platform",
@@ -3705,8 +3705,33 @@ pub const Transfer = struct {
                 "accept-encoding",
                 "accept-language",
                 "priority",
+            } else &.{
+                "pragma",
+                "cache-control",
+                "sec-ch-ua-full-version-list",
+                "sec-ch-ua-platform",
+                "device-memory",
+                "sec-ch-ua",
+                "sec-ch-ua-model",
+                "sec-ch-ua-mobile",
+                "sec-ch-ua-bitness",
+                "sec-ch-ua-arch",
+                "dpr",
+                "user-agent",
+                "sec-ch-ua-platform-version",
+                "accept",
+                "sec-fetch-site",
+                "sec-fetch-mode",
+                "sec-fetch-dest",
+                "referer",
+                "accept-encoding",
+                "accept-language",
+                "priority",
             };
             for (order) |name| {
+                if (req.request_mode != .navigate and std.ascii.eqlIgnoreCase(name, "accept") and self.findRequestHeader(name) == null) {
+                    try conn.addHeader(arena, "Accept", "*/*");
+                }
                 // A custom header suppresses curl's earlier automatic emission,
                 // while CURLOPT_ACCEPT_ENCODING still enables native decoding.
                 if (std.ascii.eqlIgnoreCase(name, "accept-encoding") and self.findRequestHeader(name) == null) {
